Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:27:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Pi as an Ask agent; OpenCode 2 answers
 alone

Pi (the person's own, with the providers they set up in it) answers Ask
behind "Other agents": no tools, no extensions, no session; the model is
picked in Settings from what "pi --list-models" names, and the answer is
read from its JSON mode (a failed attempt that Pi retries isn't an error).

OpenCode 2 answers through a background service of its own, outside
Meridian's sandbox and without its configuration, so Ask got "Agent not
found: meridian". Which OpenCode is installed is asked once in a while
(--version); 2 runs with --standalone and gets its agent and permission
rules under the keys it reads. Before 2, everything as ever.
